  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A folded, much-copied sheet of a very old song — the minstrel Marisel calls it <em>“The Green and the Grey.”</em> The verses tell of a deathless green thing that loved a raven-haired mortal youth and could not let him go when his years ran out; it waited for him past all sense, and waits still. The oldest surviving verse names him only <em>“Corin.”</em> A sad old tune, and nothing more — or so everyone who sings it believes.</p>",
